## Initial Q&A
### What specific abortion methods are legally permitted under New Zealand's Abortion Legislation Act 2020?
Answer: Under New Zealand's legal framework, abortions can be performed through either medical or surgical procedures depending on the gestation period. Specifically, the permitted methods include "early medical abortion" (taking two tablets to cause a miscarriage up to 10 weeks), "early surgical abortion" (where the "pregnancy is removed by suction" between 9 and 14-15 weeks), "later surgical abortion," "later medical abortion," and "induction of labour" (which is used for pregnancies with fetal abnormalities or for abortions after 20 weeks).

Source URL: https://www.womens-health.org.nz/health-topics/abortion-termination-of-pregnancy/

### Does New Zealand's Abortion Legislation Act 2020 permit the use of intact dilation and extraction (sometimes referred to as "partial-birth abortion")?
Answer: According to the provided source, New Zealand's Abortion Legislation Act 2020 does permit the use of intact dilation and extraction, noting that under the new law, "[t]here will be no legal restrictions on controversial methods of abortion such as intact dilation and extraction abortions (also knows as partial-birth abortions)".

Source URL: https://righttolife.org.uk/news/nz-pm-rushes-worlds-most-extreme-abortion-law-into-law-while-country-distracted-with-pandemic

### What are the gestational age limits for different abortion methods under New Zealand's Abortion Legislation Act 2020?
Answer: Under New Zealand's current abortion laws, early medical abortion is available "up to 10 weeks of pregnancy," while early surgical abortion is an option "between 9 and 14-15 weeks." For later stages of gestation up to 20 weeks, abortions may be performed by "later surgical abortion or later medical abortion," or by "early induction of labour" if there are fetal abnormalities. For pregnancies "more than 20 weeks," abortions must be managed by a team of health practitioners and are "performed by induction of labour."

Source URL: https://www.womens-health.org.nz/health-topics/abortion-termination-of-pregnancy/

### Does New Zealand's Abortion Legislation Act 2020 allow for abortion up to birth, and if so, under what specific medical and legal criteria?
Answer: Yes, under New Zealand's liberalized abortion law, abortion is legal up to birth. For pregnancies beyond 20 weeks, a qualified health practitioner may only provide abortion services if they "reasonably believes that the abortion is clinically appropriate in the circumstances." In making this determination, the practitioner must consult with at least one other qualified health practitioner and consider "all relevant legal, professional, and ethical standards," though this consultation requirement does not apply in the event of a medical emergency.

Source URL: https://fli.org.nz/life-faith-family-resources/abortion/nz-abortion-law/

### Are there any legal restrictions or bans on specific surgical abortion techniques within New Zealand's statutory framework as of the passage of the Abortion Legislation Act 2020?
Answer: Based on the provided text, there are "no legal restrictions on controversial methods of abortion such as intact dilation and extraction abortions (also knows as partial-birth abortions)" within New Zealand's statutory framework following the passage of the Abortion Legislation Act 2020.

